# .gitattributes - keep a clone byte-identical to what was committed.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#   This is a Windows / PowerShell project and the repository deliberately contains a MIX of
#   CRLF and LF files. Worse, several .ps1 files MUST keep their UTF-8 BOM: PowerShell 5.1
#   reads a BOM-less file as ANSI, the Chinese comments turn into mojibake and the parser dies
#   with a misleading "missing closing parenthesis". Any end-of-line conversion or encoding
#   smudge on checkout can therefore break the project on a machine that is not this one.
#
#   So: no conversion in either direction. What was committed is exactly what you get, on every
#   platform. A line-ending normalisation would also rewrite every stored blob once, turning a
#   one-line fix into an unreviewable diff.
#
#   If you add a file, keep its bytes as-is; tts\check_ps1.ps1 fixes the BOM when it is missing.
* -text
